Local kernel patches
====================

Patches in this directory apply on top of the pinned Perpetua commit
(scripts/fetch-perpetua.sh), in lexical order, with `git apply --index`, and
the build fails loudly when one stops applying.

A kernel patch is licensed like the file it changes (the kernel's own rule,
Documentation/process/license-rules.rst): the driver and sound patches here
modify GPL-2.0-only files and are GPL-2.0-only (LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt);
the device-tree patches (0001, 0003, 0005, 0022–0024, 0026) modify files that
carry `SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause` — Qualcomm's `kaanapali.dtsi` and
the Denial project's board file `kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts` (map220v) —
and are BSD-3-Clause. Authorship is the `From:` line of each patch; the
`Signed-off-by:` lines are the Developer Certificate of Origin (DCO 1.1) of
the people who wrote or carried it, which is what the kernel and Perpetua
require instead of a contributor agreement.

Policy, inherited from both parent projects:

- The first response to a missing feature is a patch *to Perpetua upstream*
  (github.com/denialwm/linux-perpetua), not a file here. This directory is
  for what upstream has not merged yet, carried with its submission status
  (docs/upstreaming.md), and for genuinely Ubuntu-specific needs upstream
  would rightly reject.
- Never a fix imported from a vendor kernel because it exists there; the
  device's downstream kernel is a reference for what the hardware needs,
  never a base (Perpetua devices/README states the same rule).
- Every patch names its origin and its exit condition in its header: merged
  upstream (drop on the next pin bump) or permanent (say why).

Provenance
----------

| Patches | Origin | Author | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0001, 0002 | this port (boot chain) | John Stockdale | 0001 is Ubuntu-specific (initramfs-tools reads `panic=`); 0002 to be offered upstream |
| 0003, 0008 | Fedora iceland port, github.com/mzakamin-hub/iceland-linux patch queue | mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com> | carried verbatim with their sign-off |
| 0004, 0005, 0006, 0007, 0010 | this port (C2 touch, C3 radios) | John Stockdale | to be offered upstream |
| 0009 | Fedora iceland port, re-diffed against our tree | mzak (original); re-diff by this port | drop when Perpetua carries the stock porch |
| 0011–0024 | Fedora iceland port's TDM speaker chain (AudioReach TDM endpoint, PRM TDM clocks, channel maps, sc8280xp TDM back end, TFA9865 stock setup, volume clamp, iceland DT) | mzak | carried with their sign-off where the original had one (0011 had none) |
| 0025, 0026 | infiniti-mainline (OnePlus 15, same SoC): GPR callback before probe, 1024-byte GPR intent | Victor Fuentes <victor@vlinkz.dev> | carried with their sign-off |
| 0027 | this port: revert of Perpetua aad249d15433 (tx-macro capture mutes) | John Stockdale | the revert restores upstream v7.3 behaviour on this codec |
| 0028 | this port: q6apm READ/WRITE_DONE payload-size fix (microphones, WCD playback) | John Stockdale | READ_DONE half **merged upstream independently** on 2026-11-02 (Perpetua 9ba37ef1db70, same approach; also Reixo0/linux fcabe5fd25c7) — drop that hunk at the next pin bump; the WRITE_DONE half is offered as a consistency patch, docs/upstreaming.md |
| 0029, 0030, 0032–0036 | Qualcomm's kaanapali iris (VPU) series, carried by infiniti-mainline and the Fedora iceland queue (`/srv/ubuntu-iceland/ref/iceland-linux/patches/0001-infiniti` 0033, 0035, 0032, 0034, 0037, 0038, 0036) | Vikash Garodia, Jingyi Wang, Wangao Wang, Vishnu Reddy (oss.qualcomm.com), sign-offs kept | drop when Perpetua carries the iris support (none at b7d639cfb282) |
| 0031 | this port: board enable for the iris codec (firmware-name vpu40_2v.mbn, status okay) — BSD-3-Clause (board dts) | John Stockdale | to be offered upstream with the series |
| 0037 | Fedora iceland port's "give the pen its tablet capabilities" (0036), adapted to our DT-property probe: BTN_STYLUS/2, axis resolution from touchscreen-x-mm/y-mm | mzak (original); adaptation by this port | offer with 0039 to Perpetua |
| 0038 | this port: touchscreen-x-mm/y-mm in the controller frame (193/274) — BSD-3-Clause (board dts) | John Stockdale | to be offered upstream |
| 0039 | this port: the pen reports through touchscreen_report_pos like the finger (coordinates were raw) | John Stockdale | to be offered upstream |
| 0040 | this port: the controller's pen scanning is off after every firmware download until the host sends the extended command 0x7F/0x10 (+ uplink-timing byte); the constants and sequence come from OnePlus's vendor driver for this SoC (OnePlusOSS sm8850 modules, GPL-2.0 vendor code — read, not copied); module parameter pen_type for flights | John Stockdale | flown on #43 (controller acknowledges; the pen itself still silent — research in progress); to be offered upstream with 0037/0039 |
| 0041 | this port: OPP pen handshake plumbing — the controller's uplink frames kept out of the touch parser and exposed as sysfs `pen_uplink` (+ uevent), the downlink commands (0x7F 0x40 family) accepted through `pen_downlink` with stock's gate, `pen_debug` for the bench; protocol facts from the vendor driver, nothing copied | John Stockdale | written 2026-11-02 for ladder A.3c N1/N2/N5; first flight = module swap on #44 |
| 0043–0045 | infiniti-mainline iris fixes 0069–0071 (MVP NoC low-power release on vpu4x, hierarchical-B only, no picture state on decoder input) | Victor Fuentes | drop when Perpetua carries them |
| 0046–0055 | Fedora iceland port's iris fixes 0157–0160, 0246–0250, 0292 (iova restrict region, capture bit-depth validation, hfi_sys_ops guard, uc_region boot failure, AHB bridge reset, power-off ordering, core lock, open limit, instance refcount, SMPTE 170M signalling) | Vishnu Reddy, Dmitry Baryshkov, mzak | drop as Perpetua picks them up |
| 0056–0062 | pen charger (Maxic MT5806) from the Fedora iceland port with its prerequisites (PMH0101 level-shifter regulators 0084/0085, pmic_glink hboost client 0090 adapted to our compatible, binding 0091, driver 0092, board DT 0093 re-diffed, s2idle fix 0179) | mzak; adaptations by this port | promoted into the series for build #44 (2026-11-02); flight gate in docs/bringup-plan.md (#44 row); drop as Perpetua picks them up |

Numbering note: the number 0029 was first used on 2026-11-02 for infiniti's
ADSP reserved-memory change (0x4c00000 -> 0x5000000) and withdrawn the same
day — the OnePlus board file already deletes and redefines that node with
0x5000000, so it had no effect here (docs/porting-log.md, "0029 was a
no-op"). The number was then reused for the iris platform data.
